00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.510
<b>- Color-changing 
water 
- Slime 
- Air cannon 
- Hydroponics 
Display 
- Cartesian diver</b>

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.510
<b>Dumplings</b>

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.510
<b>Wind
 Ensemble Club</b>

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.510
<b>Concert</b>

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.510
<b>Time Schedule:</b>

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.510
<b>Class 3-E 
Movie 
Screening</b>

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:27.520
<b>Performance 
Performance: Handbells 
Movie: "The Day is Long, Walk on Boy" 
Chorus</b>

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:32.520
<b>Year 3 | Chorus 
Theater Society | Play: "And Everyone Is Part of the ABC Tragedy Case File!" 
Closing Ceremony</b>

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:41.550
S-So this is a culture festival!

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.280
You're too impressed.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:44.790
Hey!

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:48.820
Where are Mayu-chan and the landlady?

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:52.040
Mayu-chan's class is 
about to open their maid café.

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:55.800
And Chiaki-senpai said she had 
a meeting with Ruriko-sensei.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.990
That's too bad.

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:00.550
I wanted us all to eat these together.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:01.840
All of that?

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.730
Did you just buy everything you could carry?

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:04.740
No!

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:05.180
Oh?

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:09.430
This is my own selection of the 
best of culture festival gourmet!

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:13.940
Just look at this grilled chicken skewer!

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:18.400
This is made with free-range chicken meat 
provided by a local farm.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:21.070
The meat's savory flavor 
and texture are exquisite.

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:25.950
And the flavor of the tamari soy sauce 
in the glaze is delectable!

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:28.200
Th-That looks delicious!

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.210
And this yakisoba!

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:34.960
This was delivered directly from a town 
that's famous for its B-grade cuisine!

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:38.340
The crispy bean sprouts create 
a perfect balance of textures!

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:43.470
And just look at this takoyaki!

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:46.180
It was made by a transfer student 
straight from Kansai.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:50.130
Fluffy on the outside, gooey on the inside...
 it's a true masterpiece!

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:51.920
The moment you eat one...

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:54.930
A glorious harmony fills your mouth!

00:11:56.740 --> 00:11:57.430
Um...

00:11:57.430 --> 00:11:58.110
Oh?

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:01.240
You keep talking about how they taste.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.110
Have you eaten all these already?

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:04.990
Of course!

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:09.120
I spent all morning conquering 
every single food stall!

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:09.120
<b>Seaweed</b>

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:11.620
What? A-All of them?

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:14.150
Just what kind of stomach do you have?

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:17.130
Delicious!

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:18.210
Isn't it?

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:20.510
Yeah, this is pretty good.

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:23.030
I'm glad you like it.

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:26.390
It's not a culture festival if you 
don't enjoy the food stall cuisine.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:30.260
I don't think there are many 
other students who've taken it this far...

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:32.180
Aside from the stalls,

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.940
you also can't miss the cafés 
and other shops run by the classes.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.760
Oh, like Mayu-chan's maid café!

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:38.360
Yes.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.860
I've already checked all of those out, too.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:47.490
<b>Maid Café</b>

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:47.490
<b>Recommended 
Pancake and
 Omelet Rice Combo</b>

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:45.060
Wow! They have a pancake 
and omelet rice combo!

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:48.050
That's the most important item 
on their menu.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:49.740
Let's go eat there next.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:52.740
I can't wait!

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:55.370
Wait, you two can still eat more?

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:57.880
So delicious!

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:01.020
Y-You're right. This is pretty good, too.

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:04.880
But should we really be spending 
all our time doing this?

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:07.650
Our play is in the evening.

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:09.140
It's still a while off.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.320
That's right.

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:13.350
Besides, we practiced until 
really late last night.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:19.060
But I feel a little uneasy...

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.620
You're a real worrywart, Hina-chan.

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:24.520
You got all your lines perfect yesterday.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.740
I guess we have no choice, then.

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:31.830
Why don't we run through 
just the opening lines?

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:36.670
Greetings, everyone.

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:39.430
Welcome to our mansion.

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:41.420
If you'll pardon me.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:44.800
And who is this young lady?

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:48.470
Hina-chan?

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:49.800
Hinako?

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:53.430
Huh? Is it my turn?

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.930
<b>Personnel 
Only 
Beyond 
This Point</b>

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:55.930
H-How could you forget the first scene?

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:58.760
We practiced that part over and over!

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:59.720
Sorry!

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:03.070
Is something wrong?

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:06.190
Actually, after practice ended yesterday,

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:09.200
I tried to check out 
everyone else's parts...

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.560
Someone here is the culprit.

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:11.700
Y-You don't mean...

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:11.700
And...

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:16.650
Reading all those lines 
made you forget your own?

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:17.710
Maybe...

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:19.460
What?!

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.330
<b>Acting</b>

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:22.090
You read something new 
and forgot the old stuff?

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:24.460
<b>Everyone Else's Lines</b>

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:24.460
Is your brain a noodle press or what?!

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:27.130
S-Sorry...

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:28.250
Now that you mention it,

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:31.470
there was a food stall with 
really good tokoroten noodles...

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:42.940
There they are.

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:46.110
Now everyone is here.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:54.290
I-I'm gonna be so nervous...

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:56.370
You're getting nervous after all we've done?

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:57.770
You'll be fine.

00:14:56.720 --> 00:15:00.000
No, I'm not the culprit...

00:14:57.770 --> 00:15:00.000
We just practiced again earlier, didn't we?

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:00.000
All wrong!

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:00.870
Yeah...

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:04.630
You'll have Yua-sama to 
back you up on the stage, too,

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:07.130
so all you need to do 
is act with confidence.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:09.010
Yua-chan...

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:11.510
I'll support you as much as I can, too.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:13.030
Kuu-chan...

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:47.270
Greetings, everyone.

00:15:47.270 --> 00:15:49.460
Welcome to our mansion.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:51.260
If you'll pardon me.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:55.140
And who is this young lady?

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:04.690
Hello.

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.880
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:21.330
<i>Sheesh... I feel like the mother 
of a child who's a real handful.</i>

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:28.030
I never thought an incident 
like this would happen...

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:32.220
<i>Hinako's acting has gotten much better.</i>

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:35.720
Someone here is the culprit!

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:39.310
And this handkerchief is 
the greatest evidence of that.

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:44.630
<i>Oh, no! I was so distracted by Hinako,</i>

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:46.440
<i>I forgot to pick it up!</i>

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:50.340
<i>The handkerchief!</i>

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.660
Oh? Where is this handkerchief?

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:58.450
Does anyone have a handkerchief?

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:00.950
It appears the lady has misplaced it.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:09.210
M-Miss...

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:12.460
This is the handkerchief you're looking for.

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:23.530
Here you go.

00:17:23.530 --> 00:17:26.490
Oh, thank you, Miss Maid!

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:27.980
You're quite welcome.

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:34.650
I'll return it after the play, okay?

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:38.740
Is this the handkerchief you lost?

00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:47.270
Yes, it is.

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:54.380
Yes, this handkerchief is 
the greatest evidence of all!

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:56.020
Thank goodness.

00:17:54.710 --> 00:18:00.690
The scent of the perfume on this 
handkerchief tells us who the culprit is.

00:17:56.020 --> 00:17:58.640
Looks like they managed 
to get back on track.

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:00.330
If it came to it,

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:04.270
I was about to ad-lib 
running out there to take it to her.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:03.410
Does anyone recognize this scent?

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:07.270
Uh, no, you'd ruin the play's setting.

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:15.280
<i>Seeing everyone acting on a stage 
makes them seem like different people.</i>

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:18.240
<i>The colorful spotlights,</i>

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:19.660
<i>the gorgeous costumes,</i>

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:22.160
<i>the speech patterns 
they don't normally use...</i>

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:25.910
<i>They all look like they're having fun, 
and they're shining.</i>

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:30.420
<i>And to think that I'm speaking 
in front of all these people...</i>

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:33.510
<i>I feel like a different person, too.</i>

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:37.170
In the short time 
since I came to this island,

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:40.620
many people have passed away.

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:47.510
But there is still something truly 
precious that I wish to protect.

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:47.510
<i>I never knew it'd be so fun 
to speak in front of people!</i>

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:50.690
Yes, that something is within my heart.

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:02.010
This concludes all of today's performances.

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:04.740
Thank you for joining us.

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:16.980
<i>It's like what happened earlier 
was just a dream...</i>

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:17.920
Hinako...

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:20.270
Oh? Yua-chan?

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:22.840
Um... I'm sorry about before.

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:25.600
I acted so stuck-up toward you,

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:26.830
then I messed up myself.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:28.260
Don't worry about that.

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:30.480
All's well that ends well!

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:33.350
Come on, let's go 
to the after-party together!

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:43.040
Hinako... thanks.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:53.230
That aside,

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:55.920
you're so cute when 
you're being honest with yourself.

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:59.220
Wh-What are you saying?! I'm always cute!

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:01.630
Hinako-san, Yua-san.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.640
Your acting was wonderful.

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:04.970
Ruri-chan!

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:06.140
I'm sorry!

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:09.550
I ruined the script you wrote.

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:12.890
Sometimes accidents are a necessary spice.

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:15.930
That was the kind of wonderful ad-lib 
you can only see on a stage.

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:17.520
I was deeply moved.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.400
Thanks!

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:22.880
The truth is, if this 
production was successful,

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:26.340
I had planned to formally start up 
the theater club again.

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:27.380
Then...

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:28.160
Yes.

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:31.540
The theater club will have 
its new start tomorrow.

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.140
On that note, Hinako-san...

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:38.540
Would you like to make 
your show business debut?

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:40.080
What?!

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:41.840
Let's star on TV together!

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:44.550
That's far too aggressive!

00:20:45.130 --> 00:20:46.800
She can't, Sensei.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.160
Kuu-chan?

00:20:48.590 --> 00:20:52.310
Hina-chan will be working hard 
with Hitotose from now on!

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:53.920
Hitotose?

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:56.810
It's a theater troupe we started 
with our apartment's tenants.

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:58.820
I'm the principal.

00:20:59.090 --> 00:21:02.420
We haven't put on a 
performance yet, though...

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:03.320
I see.

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:05.680
Is there anything I can help with?

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:06.800
You'll help us?

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:10.850
Supporting club members in their 
activities is part of an advisor's job.

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:12.580
I-I'll help, too!

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.500
It scares me to think of 
Hinako as the principal.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:17.750
Thanks for worrying about us!

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:20.840
I-I never said I was worried!

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:23.720
Hey, guys!

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:26.720
The after-party is starting!

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.320
Coming!

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:30.350
Well, shall we go?

00:21:30.660 --> 00:21:32.620
Now that our troupe has grown,

00:21:32.620 --> 00:21:34.730
let's do our best to make it to Suzuran.

00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:36.130
Yeah!

00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:39.980
<i>I was so worried when I first came to Tokyo,</i>

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:44.610
<i>but maybe I've gotten just 
a little closer to who I want to be.</i>

00:21:45.060 --> 00:21:46.660
Come on, let's get moving.

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:48.610
Hina-chan, let's go.

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:50.100
Okay!

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:36.430
<b>The Lost Swimsuit</b>

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:31.170
My choice to cast Hinako-san 
as the heroine was not a mistake.

00:23:31.170 --> 00:23:33.400
For our next performance, 
how about a show in summer,

00:23:33.400 --> 00:23:37.200
taking place at the beach, 
and starring girls in swimsuits?

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:39.270
Next time, "The Lost Swimsuit."
